[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2016-06-30T23:32:47Z","updated_at":"2016-07-07T11:20:02Z","closed_at":"2016-07-07T11:20:02Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Most maven jars work just fine, but I've run into a few that generate an incorrect WORKSPACE. For example:\n\n```\n% ./output/bazel run //src/tools/generate_workspace -- --artifact=com.puppycrawl.tools:checkstyle:jar:6.11.2\n\nINFO: Running command line: bazel-bin/src/tools/generate_workspace/generate_workspace '--artifact=com.puppycrawl.tools:checkstyle:jar:6.11.2'\nWrote:\n/tmp/1467328940834-0/WORKSPACE\n/tmp/1467328940834-0/BUILD\n```\n\n```\n% tail -n 8 /tmp/1467328940834-0/WORKSPACE\n\n# com.puppycrawl.tools:checkstyle:jar:6.11.2\nmaven_jar(\n    name = \"antlr_antlr\",\n    artifact = \"antlr:antlr:2.7.7\",\n    sha1 = \"83cd2cd674a217ade95a4bb83a8a14f351f48bd0  /home/maven/repository-staging/to-ibiblio/maven2/antlr/antlr/2.7.7/antlr-2.7.7.jar\",\n)\n```\n\nAs you can see, it somehow put a path into the `sha1` field. I'm running latest master:\n\n```\n% ./output/bazel version\nAnother command is running (pid = 16736).  Waiting for it to complete...\nBuild label: 0.3.0-2016-06-30 (@a18add1)\nBuild target: bazel-out/local-fastbuild/bin/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/bazel/BazelServer_deploy.jar\nBuild time: Thu Jun 30 23:15:38 2016 (1467328538)\nBuild timestamp: 1467328538\nBuild timestamp as int: 1467328538\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/u